---
import globalSearch from "../../captures/global-search.png";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../../site/links.ts";
---

<GuidePage manual="docs" slug="first-steps" lead="Katari comes empty. Here is how to go from setup to the first title in your library.">
  <Task id="extension-store" title="Add extensions">
    <p>
      Titles come from sources, and sources come in extensions. Add an extension store under <Path>Browse › Extensions › ⋮ › Extension
      stores</Path>, then install the extensions you want from <Path>Browse › Extensions</Path>.
      <a href={sitePath("docs/extension-stores/")}>Extension stores</a> walks through both, and what to do when an extension shows as
      <strong>Untrusted</strong>.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="find" title="Find something to read or watch" shot={{ image: globalSearch, alt: "One search finding comics, books and a film", caption: "Global search" }}>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sources</strong> lists every installed source. Open one to browse it.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Feeds</strong> follows a source's <strong>Popular</strong> or <strong>Latest</strong> list, or a filtered search saved as
        a preset, and remembers where you stopped. Add one with <strong>+</strong> on the Feeds tab.
      </li>
      <li>To search every source at once, tap <strong>Global search</strong> at the top of <Path>Browse › Sources</Path>.</li>
    </ul>
  </Task>

  <Task id="library" title="Add it to your library">
    <ol>
      <li>Open a title and tap <strong>Add to library</strong>. It now reads <strong>In library</strong>.</li>
      <li>If you have categories, Katari asks which ones to put it in.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      To skip the question, pick a category under <Path>Settings › Library › Default category</Path>. New chapters, episodes and books
      of everything in your library arrive in the <strong>Updates</strong> tab; <a href={sitePath("docs/library-updates/")}>Library
      updates</a> explains when Katari checks.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="tabs" title="Show the Translator, Statistics and Switch tabs">
    <p>
      Katari starts with Library, Updates, History, Browse and More. Translator, Statistics and Switch are hidden at first, and Switch
      only appears once you have two or more profiles.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <Path>Settings › Appearance › Home screen tabs</Path>.</li>
      <li>Press and hold a destination, then drop it where you want it.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The dock holds five tabs. Tabs you put under <strong>Overflow</strong> open from <strong>Menu</strong>, which then takes the
      fifth place. More can't be hidden.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
